<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BESH> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BESH> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Basic Experimental Studies Involving Humans — the FDA/NIH-defined category sitting BETWEEN non-human basic research and conventional clinical trials: mechanistic studies that meet the NIH clinical-trial definition (human participants, prospective assignment, intervention, biomedical outcome) but whose aim is understanding a phenomenon, not evaluating a clinical intervention. Registered and disclosed under dedicated FDA/NIH policy. Size: small; sites: academic research settings." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BESH> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BESH" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BESH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "basic experimental studies involving humans"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BESH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "basic experimental study with humans"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BiomedicalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BiomedicalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reuses CDISC Biomedical Concept anchors as an INPUT (crosswalk targets), not a rival. The concept-first pivot: bind once to the concept; every standard (SDTM/Define/FHIR) is then a projection." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BiomedicalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Biomedical Concept" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BiomedicalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Evidence> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BiomedicalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A canonical, sponsor-agnostic concept a data element binds to (e.g. Sodium). Codes to external terminologies (LOINC, NCIt, SNOMED) are attached as Relationships to dereferenceable URIs via cr:codedAs — never as string Properties." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BlindingConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BlindingConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grounded in MVP Inventory §5 blinding. A cr:blindingScope value (e.g. 'treatment-assignment', 'unblinded-pk') plus provenance." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BlindingConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Blinding Constraint" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BlindingConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Constraint> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BlindingConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The scope and provenance of what is blinded in a transfer, and to whom — a constraint that drives routing, not a boolean. Replaces the MVP's boolean 'Transfer Blinding'." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BriefingBook> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BriefingBook> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A dossier submitted to the regulator ahead of a meeting (Pre-IND / EOP2)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#BriefingBook> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Briefing Book" .
