<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataElementSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grounded in MVP Inventory content rows and the LAB v2.0 LB variable list. The SDTM target is NEVER a stored attribute here — it is a crosswalk edge rendered on projection." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataElementSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Data Element Specification" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataElementSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Scope> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataElementSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One expected data element in a TransferSpecification: it binds to a canonical BiomedicalConcept, declares its unit, value range, controlled terminology, mandatory-ness, significant digits and derived flag. The universal content pattern — one shape covers lab, ECG, imaging analytes; data-type specifics are typed extensions, not parallel hierarchies." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataManager> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataManager> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Creates and locks CRFs, manages queries, reconciles lab and date data, and manages data transfers. Dual-lens: sees CRF as data source for analysis (sponsor perspective)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataManager> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Data Manager" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataManager> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/hcls/v1#Person> .
