<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataTransferAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "vendor data agreement"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataTransferAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The governing artifact for a vendor-to-sponsor transfer relationship. Packages one or more TransferSpecifications, references a TransferProfile, is ratified by Attestations, and cites the conformance shapes it must satisfy. Versioned (DNA status + bitemporal)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataTransferAgreement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Data Transfer Agreement"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bitemporal: the lock's valid time (top:observedAt) is the lock date; corrections are new assertions, never rewrites." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Database Lock" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Evidence> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Versioned> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "DB lock"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "data lock"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "hard lock"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "soft lock"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The act of freezing the study database. A SOFT lock freezes it for review and is reversible; a HARD lock freezes it for analysis. After a hard lock, no clinical value may change without a recorded DatabaseUnlock." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Database Lock"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseLock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Operators say 'the finish line'; soft vs hard is carried by cr:lockType, not by separate classes (ADR-0024 one-question gate: a classification, not a kind)."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Database Unlock" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Evidence> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Versioned> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "database reopen"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "unlock"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A controlled, reasoned reopening of a locked database (e.g. a late data correction). It references the DatabaseLock it reopens and records a reason — the audit gate that makes post-lock change legitimate rather than silent." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DatabaseUnlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Database Unlock"@en .
