<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Operational and leading, in contrast to the trial-level cr:QualityToleranceLimit which is systemic. A KRI should trace to the CtQ factor it protects (cr:informsFactor) — a KRI with no CtQ ancestry is measurement theater." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Key Risk Indicator" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Constraint> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "KRI"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "quality metric"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "risk indicator"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A site- or data-domain-level leading metric used to detect localized performance degradation early — screen-failure rate, eCRF entry cycle time, query aging, deviation rate. Breaches trigger targeted monitoring intervention, not (by themselves) CSR reporting." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KeyRiskIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Key Risk Indicator"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The kit number is what the site sees; the arm behind it stays with the randomization system. Dispensing (cr:DispensingEvent, supply module) cites the kit." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Kit Assignment" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Temporal> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Versioned> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "blinded kit"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "kit number"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "kit"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The assignment of a blinded kit (numbered container of investigational product or comparator) to a randomized participant — the mechanism that operationalizes the blind." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hiddenLabel> "IRT"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hiddenLabel> "IWRS"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hiddenLabel> "IxRS"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hiddenLabel> "RTSM"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Kit Assignment"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#KitAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "IxRS / IWRS / IRT / RTSM name the SYSTEM that performs randomization and supply; its recorded acts are cr:RandomizationEvent and cr:KitAssignment."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#LabOrder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#LabOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The order binding an assay to a specimen — what the operator calls 'the order'. Renamed from cr:AnalysisRequest: 'analysis request' collides with every non-lab sense of analysis (e.g. a manager asking for a site-performance analysis) — first-principles P2, ADR-0024 ambiguity gate." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#LabOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lab Order" .
