<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Purpose: initial human safety, tolerability, dosing (dose escalation, MTD), and pharmacokinetics — not efficacy. Size: small (typically 20–100), healthy volunteers or, in oncology, patients. Sites: specialized Phase-1 units with intensive-monitoring capability, usually a handful. Device-world names: feasibility / pilot / early feasibility study." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Phase 1" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "FIH"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "early feasibility study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "early-stage study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "feasibility study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "first-in-human"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "phase I"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "pilot study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Purpose: preliminary efficacy signal and dose selection (dose-ranging; ends at the EOP2 gate this model treats as the analysis decision node), continued safety. Size: moderate (typically 100–300 patients with the condition). Sites: academic and specialty investigative sites, tens of sites." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Phase 2" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dose-finding study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "phase II"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "proof-of-concept study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Purpose: confirmatory efficacy and safety versus control — the evidence a marketing application rests on. Size: large (typically 300–3,000+). Sites: broad multi-site, multi-region networks including community sites. Device-world name: pivotal study (the pre-market confirmatory trial, akin to a Phase 3 drug trial)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Phase 3" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "confirmatory trial"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "late-stage study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "phase III"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "pivotal study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "pre-market pivotal study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3Design> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3Design> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A proposed Phase 3 trial design taken to the EOP2 meeting." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3Design> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Proposed Phase 3 Design" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase3Design> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Scope> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Purpose: real-world safety and effectiveness after approval — rare adverse events, long-term outcomes, use in broader populations; often a post-marketing commitment. Size: large to very large. Sites: routine-care settings. Device-world name: post-market surveillance study." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Phase 4" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase4> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "PMS study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase4> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "phase IV"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase4> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "post-market surveillance study"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Phase4> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "post-marketing study"@en .
