<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Trial-level, few in number (TransCelerate: 3-5 per trial — see QTLCountShape), defined before first participant first visit, monitored continuously, and every significant deviation documented in the CSR (cr:reportedIn). Site-level leading metrics are cr:KeyRiskIndicator, a different concept." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Quality Tolerance Limit" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Constraint> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "QTL"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "acceptable range"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "quality tolerance level"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A trial-level boundary on a quality parameter tied to a critical-to-quality factor — the range beyond which a systemic issue threatens participant safety, data integrity, or the study's statistical power. ICH E6(R3) calls these acceptable ranges; the industry says QTL." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#QualityToleranceLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Quality Tolerance Limit"@en .
