<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Timing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Timing" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#Timing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Constraint> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TimingWindow> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TimingWindow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An allowed tolerance around a planned time: a lower and an upper offset in days (e.g. [-2 days, +2 days])." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TimingWindow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Timing Window" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TimingWindow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Constraint> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrainingRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrainingRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Document> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Amendment as event (Outcome:StatusChange). Bitemporal; drives the cross-entity shape that forces amendment propagation to be explicit." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Transfer Amendment" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Outcome> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Versioned> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferAmendment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A status change on a protocol/spec version that carries effectiveFrom/To and MUST reference the TransferSpecifications it affects. Propagation is a graph update + re-validation, not N manual DTA re-authorings." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferFile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferFile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grounded in the info-model TRANSFER_FILE entity. The specification is the plan; the file is the Outcome:Artifact." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferFile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Transfer File" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferFile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Outcome> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferFile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Versioned> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferFile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An actual delivered file instance (as distinct from its TransferSpecification). Carries its own transfer lifecycle timestamps and PROV attribution to the vendor org." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grounded in MVP Inventory §5 'File Transfer Information'. Specialized per vendor as cr:VendorConnectorProfile instances grounded in each vendor's public API/export surface." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Transfer Profile" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Scope> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The operational envelope of a transfer: file format, delimiter, encoding, transmission method, transmission type (cumulative vs incremental), schedule, provider/receiver folder, environment. A declaration (top:Scope); its validity is enforced by cr:TransferProfile* SHACL shapes (open Q2: Scope for declaration + Constraint shapes for enforcement)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferScope> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferScope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grounded in DTA MVP Information Model open Q1 (multi-vendor / multi-scope DTA). Recommend modeling scope explicitly — the single-vendor simplification is exactly where the exponential hides." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferScope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Transfer Scope" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferScope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Scope> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferScope> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mediator that lets one DataTransferAgreement cover multiple vendor/data-type scopes without repeating the agreement. Each TransferScope binds a data type, a vendor Organization and its TransferSpecification(s). Modeling scope explicitly from the start is where the DTA group's combinatorics are made visible rather than hidden (open Q1)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grounded in the info-model TRANSFER_SPECIFICATION entity and CDISC LAB Model v2.0 content. Placed under top:Scope (a specification/plan), bitemporal so amendments supersede cleanly." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Transfer Specification" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Scope> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Versioned> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TransferSpecification> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The content layer (the DTS): the set of DataElementSpecifications to be delivered for a given data type/vendor under a DataTransferAgreement. A plan for content, not an act." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialLifecycle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialLifecycle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The root stage encompassing the entire lifespan of a clinical trial from protocol design to study archival." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialLifecycle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Clinical Trial Lifecycle" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialLifecycle> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#containsStage> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#CloseoutStage> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialLifecycle> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#containsStage> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#ConductStage> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialLifecycle> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#containsStage> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#StartupStage> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://www.ich.org/page/efficacy-guidelines> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trial Master File" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Evidence> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "TMF" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "TMF"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "eTMF"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The collection of essential records that allows the conduct of the trial and the quality of the data to be evaluated (paraphrased, ICH E6(R3))." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialMasterFile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Trial Master File"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Carried on the study as cr:trialPhase -> one of the named individuals below (ADR-0024: a classification rides as a value/individual, never a subclass of Study). Each phase carries the names practitioners actually use — including the device-world names, per the in-model devices decision (BOUNDARIES.md). USDM: StudyVersion.studyPhase is the crosswalk target." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trial Phase" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Scope> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialPhase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The regulatory development phase a clinical trial belongs to — the answer to 'what kind of trial is this?' (Phase 1, 2, 3, 4, or BESH). A classification of the study itself, not a position in its execution (that is the lifecycle stage)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Stages form a containment tree (cr:containsStage) and a precedence chain (cr:precedesStage). Actions bind to stages via cr:occursInStage. CR-owned deliberately: trial stages exist only in clinical research, so this does not live in hcls-core." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trial Stage" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Scope> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "lifecycle stage"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "study stage"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#TrialStage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A bounded, sequenced stage of a clinical trial's execution lifecycle — the answer to 'where in its run is this trial?' (startup, conduct, closeout, and their named sub-stages). A position in the trial's execution, not a classification of the study (that is the trial phase)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Modeled like cr:DatabaseUnlock: the blind is never silently broken. An unblinding must carry its reason and its authorizer; one without both is a Violation. The unblinding kind (emergency vs planned) is a value, not a class (ADR-0024 one-question gate)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unblinding Event" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Temporal> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://top.scientix.ai/v1#Versioned> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "breaking the blind"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "code break"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "emergency unblinding"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "unblinding"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The controlled, audited disclosure of a participant's treatment assignment — emergency (safety) or planned (analysis milestone)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#UnblindingEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Unblinding Event"@en .
