<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#unboundRationale> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#unboundRationale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The documented reason a DataElementSpecification is deliberately NOT bound to a BiomedicalConcept — e.g. a vendor passthrough / escape-hatch column (the template's AUX1–10, CTESTCD/CTEST/CUNIT/CSPEC) for which no canonical concept yet exists. Its presence makes 'unbound' an explicit, auditable choice rather than a silent prose gap: every element is either bound (concept + UCUM unit) or explicitly unbound WITH a reason. Bind, don't describe — and when you can't bind, say why." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#unboundRationale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#DataElementSpecification> .
