<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-agent> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "First-principles P7 CV-obligations (anti-synonym example)" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-agent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-agent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "ANTI-SYNONYM: pharmacological 'agent' (the drug/substance) is NOT top:Agent (an actor bearing responsibility). Route drug-sense to cr:InvestigationalProduct / hcls:Substance; actor-sense to top:Agent."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-agent> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "agent"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-analysis> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Convener sanity review, 2026-07 (cr-core-lims ambiguity finding)" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: a laboratory assay (cr:AssayDefinition / cr:LabOrder), the statistical analysis layer (cr:AnalysisDataset / cr:AnalysisDecision / SAP), and everyday operational analysis ('analyze the five worst sites'). Never route the bare word; qualify by context — lab context -> assay terms, biostatistics context -> analysis-layer terms, otherwise no routing."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-analysis> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "analysis"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-arm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "OPMODEL §1.1 Study Design" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-arm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-arm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: treatment arm (cr:Arm) vs the anatomical arm (blood-draw laterality, injection site). Study-design context routes to cr:Arm; clinical-procedure context is anatomical."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-arm> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "arm"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-monitor> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "OPMODEL §2.5 Oversight; ROLES persona aliases" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-monitor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-monitor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: the person (cr:ClinicalResearchAssociate), the visit (monitoring visit), the discipline (risk-based / central / medical monitoring — distinct capabilities), and the verb. Default routing: the CRA role; qualify otherwise."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-monitor> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "monitor"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-participant-patient> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Industry drift observed by convener, 2026-07 (ADR-0024): 'There are indications that the industry is moving to patient, but for clinical research, participant should be the preferred label.'" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-participant-patient> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-participant-patient> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Routed to cr:StudySubject in study context; routed to hcls:Person in care-delivery context."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-participant-patient> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "patient"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-phase> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Convener sanity review, 2026-07 (cr-core-phases conflation finding)" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-phase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-phase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: the trial phase (cr:TrialPhase — Phase 1..4 / BESH, a classification of the STUDY: 'this is a Phase 2 trial') vs the trial stage (cr:TrialStage — startup/conduct/closeout, a position in the trial's EXECUTION). Neither concept uses the bare word: the model only names the qualified forms (trial phase, trial stage); any new label containing 'phase' must route explicitly."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-phase> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "phase"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-screen> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "OPMODEL §2.2 Recruitment" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-screen> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-screen> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: eligibility screening (the recruitment-funnel activity — vocabulary lands with the funnel model, a declared V1 deferral) vs screen failure vs the UI screen. No default routing; qualify."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-screen> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "screen"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-service> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Convener sanity review, 2026-07 (cr-core-lims ambiguity finding)" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-service> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-service> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: a catalog lab test (cr:AssayDefinition, formerly 'AnalysisService'), a vendor organization (cr:ServiceProvider), and the API/runtime sense. Default routing: none; qualify."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-service> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "service"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-site> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "OPMODEL §1.4 Site Selection" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-site> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-site> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: the investigative site (cr:StudySite, an organization) vs bfo:Site / top:Location (a place) vs injection/body site vs website. Default routing in this domain: cr:StudySite."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-site> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "site"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-subject> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "First-principles P7 CV-obligations (homonym-routing example); OPMODEL" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-subject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#Label> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-subject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "HOMONYM: human-research 'subject' routes to cr:StudySubject (prefLabel Participant, ADR-0024); animal-research 'subject' is out of this domain; grammatical/email 'subject' is noise. Never route to hcls:Person."@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#xl-subject> <http://www.w3.org/2008/05/skos-xl#literalForm> "subject"@en .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1#yieldsDesign> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
