<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/actions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The authorized-operation layer: 78 hcls:Action archetypes (who may do what, in which trial stage, on what) grounding agent authorization queries." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/actions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — action catalog" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/actions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/adam> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "ADaM's value is reproducibility: every analysis result traces to its source. In this reference the chain is result -> analysis dataset -> NATIVE source facts (via W3C PROV wasDerivedFrom) — traceability to the one source of truth, not the fragile SDTM-document -> ADaM-document chain. SDTM and ADaM are both views of the native graph. v1.1 adds the CDISC ADaM structural vocabulary: the dataset's structure class (ADSL / BDS / OCCDS — a CLASSIFICATION carried as a value, ADR-0024) and the analysis variable / parameter layer (PARAMCD) that BDS datasets pivot on." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/adam> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — ADaM analysis layer & traceability" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/adam> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/adam> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.1" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/coding> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The coding WORKFLOW the term crosswalks alone don't carry (Operating Model §3.2): a code assignment is a promoted JUDGMENT — 'this verbatim term means this dictionary code' — with its method (autocoder vs manual), its coder, and its review. The existing cr:meddra* properties record WHERE an event landed in MedDRA; this module records WHO decided that, HOW, and whether a human reviewed it. WHODrug joins MedDRA as a BYOL (bring-your-own-license) IRI reference — no licensed content is reproduced. NOTICE: MedDRA is © MSSO/ICH; WHODrug is © Uppsala Monitoring Centre; both require valid licences to resolve." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/coding> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — medical coding workflow (MedDRA / WHODrug)" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/coding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/coding> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/deviation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Deviation events, antecedents, risk signals, and corrective/preventive actions — the quality-event chain." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/deviation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — protocol deviations & CAPA" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/deviation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/disclosure> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Two submission-and-transparency layers the CSR/eCTD spine didn't carry (Operating Model §3.4): (1) the Integrated Summaries of Safety and Efficacy (ISS/ISE) — cross-study analyses that rest on the per-study locked datasets; the summary KIND is a value, not a class (ADR-0024). (2) The public-disclosure obligations: the trial-registry record (ClinicalTrials.gov / EUCTR — registration, results posting) and publications. Disclosure artifacts are projections of already-produced results, never new sources of truth — the same manifest discipline as the eCTD." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/disclosure> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — integrated summaries & disclosure" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/disclosure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/disclosure> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/edc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Electronic data capture: eCRF, clinical observations, queries, source data verification." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/edc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — EDC & clinical observations" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/edc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/eop2> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The EOP2 gate: analysis decisions, briefing evidence, go/no-go conclusions." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/eop2> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — End-of-Phase-2 decision" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/eop2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/gcp> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights> "Independent derivative adaptation of the ICH E6(R3) Guideline. The classes, properties, and SKOS concepts here are an adaptation (structure + paraphrased definitions), not a reproduction. NOT endorsed or sponsored by ICH. The original ICH E6(R3) document is copyright © ICH." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/gcp> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ICH E6(R3) Good Clinical Practice (Step 4, adopted January 2025): Principles, Glossary, and Annex 1 (interventional trials). Annex 2 (additional/non-traditional data sources) is NOT modeled in this version." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/gcp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/gcp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Changes made: ICH E6(R3) terms are reorganized into an OWL/SKOS structure, definitions are paraphrased, and obligations are expressed as SHACL shapes rather than encoded text. Each derived term carries rdfs:isDefinedBy the ICH efficacy-guidelines source." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/gcp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TOP CR — ICH E6(R3) GCP definitional layer" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/lims> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Lab orders, assay definitions, specimens, custody chain, and assay results." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/lims> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — laboratory & specimens" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/lims> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/participant> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Extends CR-core with InformedConsent enrichment (US-500-003): consentVersion, consentFormIRI, witnessedBy, withdrawalDate. Property-only module: the classes these properties describe (cr:InformedConsent, cr:StudySubject, cr:Enrollment, cr:EligibilityCriterion) are defined once, in cr-core.ttl." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/participant> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core ontology — participant & consent module" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/participant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/participant> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.5" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/phases> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Two deliberately separated concepts: cr:TrialPhase (Phase 1-4, BESH — classification of the study) and cr:TrialStage (startup/conduct/closeout — position in execution)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/phases> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — trial phases & trial stages" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/phases> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/preind> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Pre-IND meetings, briefing books, regulatory questions and positions, the IND 30-day clock." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/preind> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — pre-IND & regulatory interactions" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/preind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/privacy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "PII boundary vocabulary: lawful bases, data categories, pseudonymization discipline." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/privacy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — privacy & lawful basis" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/privacy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/randomization> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The events an IxRS/RTSM system records, modeled as first-class bitemporal facts (Operating Model §2.3): the randomization act (subject → arm, under a stratum), the kit assignment that keeps the blind, and the audited unblinding event. The design-time ratio stays on the study (cr:randomizationRatio); these are the EXECUTION events. An unblinding without a recorded reason and authorization is the pharmacovigilance breach every inspector checks first — modeled exactly like cr:DatabaseUnlock: an audited event, never a silent state flip." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/randomization> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — randomization & blinding (IxRS/RTSM events)" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/randomization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/randomization> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/rbqm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The ICH E6(R3)/Q9(R1) RBQM cycle: CtQ factors, risk assessments, QTLs, KRIs, metric observations, limit breaches, mitigation and review." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/rbqm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — risk-based quality management" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/rbqm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/recruitment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The funnel from outreach to enrolled participant (Operating Model §2.2–2.3): campaign → candidate → pre-screening → screening → conversion. The candidate (cr:Recruit) is a SITE-BOUNDARY identity like hcls:Person — PII-side, never referenced by downstream clinical data; conversion to the pseudonymous cr:StudySubject happens only through the attested cr:Enrollment bridge. Screen failure is an OUTCOME VALUE, not a class (ADR-0024 one-question gate: a classification of a screening, not a kind of thing)." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/recruitment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — recruitment & screening funnel" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/recruitment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/recruitment> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/regulatory> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Regulatory laws and lawful bases the domain cites (ICH E6(R3), 21 CFR Part 11, GDPR) as named individuals." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/regulatory> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR — regulatory constraints" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/regulatory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/roles> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "OWL agent-type classes (site- and sponsor-boundary) and the JTBD catalog binding operator intent to authorized actions." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/roles> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — agent types & jobs-to-be-done" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/roles> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/safety> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Adverse events, SAEs, causality and expectedness assessments, expedited reporting clocks." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/safety> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — safety & pharmacovigilance" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/safety> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/schedule> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The bitemporal SoA: planned visits and activities, amendments, as-of reconstruction." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/schedule> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — schedule of activities" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/schedule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/site-closeout> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The SITE-side of closeout (Operating Model §3.1) — the counterpart of the data-side database lock: the Close-Out Visit, the reconciliations (drug, device, documents, queries — the SCOPE is a value, not four classes, ADR-0024), the Investigator Site File whose completeness gates closure, the archival with its retention clock, and the site-closure record that must rest on all of it. A closure without a Close-Out Visit and completed reconciliations is a Violation — a site is closed by evidence, not by declaration." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/site-closeout> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — site closeout" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/site-closeout> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/site-closeout> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/startup-package> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Startup artifacts, work streams, and the derivation chain from package to activation prerequisites." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/startup-package> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — study startup package" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/startup-package> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/startup> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Site activation and its prerequisites: IRB approval, CTA, SIV; enrollment-before-activation is the flagship violation." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/startup> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — site activation" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/startup> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/supply> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The investigational-product custody events (Operating Model §2.1/§2.4/§3.1): shipment to site, dispensing to a participant, return, and authorized destruction — each a first-class bitemporal event on an hcls:Lot. The ACCOUNTABILITY LOG IS A PROJECTION of these events (like the DoA log), never a maintained spreadsheet: reconcile-ability is a query over the event chain. A temperature excursion is a promoted fact that quarantines what it touched." .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/supply> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "CR-core — drug supply & IMP accountability" .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/supply> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://top.scientix.ai/cr/v1/supply> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0" .
